Rule 1 (tensor can not have an integer dtype: 1–5)
{v_1: tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∨ 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 2 (tensor can not have an bool dtype: 0)
{v_1: tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 3 (v_2 should be a valid dimension of input tensor i.e. -ndim <= v_2 <= ndim-1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= -1 × ndim(v_1) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1
>>
Rule 4 (v_2 or dim, when a tuple, should only include valid dimensions of input tensor i.e. -ndim <= v_2[i] <= ndim-1 for i in v_2)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : -1 × ndim(v_1) ≤ v_2[i] ∧ v_2[i] ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1
>>
Rule 5 (tensor can not have an complex dtype: 9 and 10)
{v_1: tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 6 (tensor v_1 and v_2 must have the same dtype)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)